WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:17.881
"Huh?" Cole said to Henry. "Where are we going?"

2
00:00:17.882 --> 00:00:26.495
Henry just started running. Cole, Maggie, and Nathan followed.

3
00:00:26.496 --> 00:00:30.266
"Hey, where are you going?" Nora appeared behind them.

4
00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:34.245
"Nowhere," Nathan called. "Go away."

5
00:00:34.246 --> 00:00:39.860
Nora ignored her brother's orders and chased after them as Henry led the way to the basket-weaving booth.

6
00:00:39.861 --> 00:00:45.614
They arrived just in time to see someone scurrying out, holding a large shopping bag.

7
00:00:45.615 --> 00:00:49.207
"Patrick!" Henry called. "Stop!"

8
00:00:49.208 --> 00:00:54.995
Patrick scowled. "What? I need to get back to the art show for the judging."

9
00:00:54.996 --> 00:00:58.105
"You're too late," Maggie informed him.

10
00:00:58.106 --> 00:01:02.779
"The judges already looked at your painting. Why weren't you there?"

11
00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:06.945
She still looked confused. So did Cole and Nathan.

12
00:01:06.946 --> 00:01:09.941
Nora wasn't paying attention to any of them.

13
00:01:09.942 --> 00:01:13.258
She was looking at some pretty baskets nearby.

14
00:01:13.259 --> 00:01:18.683
Henry stared at the shopping bag. "We heard you made a basket," he said.

15
00:01:18.684 --> 00:01:23.626
"It must be really large if you need that huge bag to carry it."

16
00:01:23.627 --> 00:01:27.208
"Yeah, so what?" Patrick glared at Henry.

17
00:01:27.209 --> 00:01:30.696
Henry smiled. "Can we see it?"

18
00:01:30.697 --> 00:01:35.893
Just then Hannah appeared. "His basket isn't large," she said.

19
00:01:35.894 --> 00:01:39.688
"He made a little round basket, just like everyone else."

20
00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:42.832
"What are you doing here?" Maggie asked her.

21
00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:45.932
"I saw you guys run off." Hannah shrugged.

22
00:01:45.933 --> 00:01:50.086
"I was curious, so I followed you. What's going on?"

23
00:01:50.087 --> 00:01:56.757
"If Patrick made a small basket, why'd you put it in such a big bag?" Henry asked Hannah.

24
00:01:56.758 --> 00:01:59.777
"That's Patrick's bag," Hannah said.

25
00:01:59.778 --> 00:02:05.091
"He told me he'd put his basket in there. He said it had extra canvases in it."

26
00:02:05.092 --> 00:02:09.870
"If that's true, maybe you should show us," Henry told Patrick.

27
00:02:09.871 --> 00:02:13.171
Patrick looked stubborn. "Why should I?

28
00:02:13.172 --> 00:02:16.231
It's none of your business what I have in my bag."

29
00:02:16.232 --> 00:02:20.980
Maggie stepped forward. "You'd better show us what's in your bag!

30
00:02:20.981 --> 00:02:25.616
And if there's a painting of a cat in there, you're going to be in big trouble!"

31
00:02:25.617 --> 00:02:30.545
Nora rushed over. "A painting of a cat?" she cried.

32
00:02:30.546 --> 00:02:37.571
"No! That's mine!" She grabbed the shopping bag out of Patrick's hand.

33
00:02:37.572 --> 00:02:39.725
"Hey!" Patrick cried.

34
00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:43.004
But Nora was already dumping out the contents.

35
00:02:43.005 --> 00:02:47.672
A tiny basket tumbled onto the ground—followed by Nathan's painting!

36
00:02:47.673 --> 00:02:53.485
"Aha!" Cole cried. "But wait. I thought Patrick had an alibi."

37
00:02:53.486 --> 00:02:55.686
"Me too," said Henry.

38
00:02:55.687 --> 00:03:01.690
"Then I realized something: Hannah told us that Patrick was in her booth.

39
00:03:01.691 --> 00:03:05.612
But she didn't say exactly when he was there.

40
00:03:05.613 --> 00:03:11.166
And I remembered he had a big bag, but probably made a tiny basket."

41
00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:18.052
He shrugged. "Besides, Patrick was the one with the best motive all along."

42
00:03:18.053 --> 00:03:23.133
Patrick's eyes looked watery. "I'm sorry, Nathan," he blurted out.

43
00:03:23.134 --> 00:03:25.970
"I really wanted my painting to be in the museum.

44
00:03:25.971 --> 00:03:30.170
When Owen told us how much the judges liked yours, I panicked."

45
00:03:30.171 --> 00:03:35.585
Patrick's parents were standing nearby. "Patrick!" his mother cried.

46
00:03:35.586 --> 00:03:38.477
"I cannot believe what I am hearing!"

47
00:03:38.478 --> 00:03:41.601
Patrick slunk over to his parents.

48
00:03:41.602 --> 00:03:45.174
While they scolded him harshly, Cole grabbed the painting.

49
00:03:45.175 --> 00:03:51.627
"We need to get this back before it's too late!"

50
00:03:51.628 --> 00:03:55.970
But when the kids arrived back at the art show, the judges were finished.

51
00:03:55.971 --> 00:04:00.491
"Wait!" Maggie cried. "We have one more painting."

52
00:04:00.492 --> 00:04:03.569
"I'm sorry, young lady," the art teacher said.

53
00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:07.431
"I'm afraid it's too late. We've already chosen the winners."

54
00:04:07.432 --> 00:04:12.251
"But it's not Nathan's fault his painting wasn't here!" Cole protested.

55
00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:16.922
The curator shook her head. "I'm sorry. We can't—"

56
00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:23.879
Suddenly Daniella stepped out of the crowd. "Perhaps I can change your minds?"

57
00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:27.520
She whipped off her red wig, revealing dark hair beneath.

58
00:04:27.521 --> 00:04:29.939
The judges all gasped.

59
00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:33.221
"Can it be?" the art teacher exclaimed.

60
00:04:33.222 --> 00:04:38.040
"It's Daniella Diaz!" the local painter cried.

61
00:04:38.041 --> 00:04:43.037
The curator looked awed. "I'd recognize her anywhere."

62
00:04:43.038 --> 00:04:47.217
Henry glanced at his friends. They looked surprised.

63
00:04:47.218 --> 00:04:51.281
"I guess she really is world famous," Cole whispered.

64
00:04:51.282 --> 00:04:54.135
"Please, dear art lovers."

65
00:04:54.136 --> 00:04:58.521
Daniella took Nathan's painting out of Cole's hands.

66
00:04:58.522 --> 00:05:02.942
"Could you include my young friend's painting in your little contest?

67
00:05:02.943 --> 00:05:06.058
I'd consider it a personal favor."

68
00:05:06.059 --> 00:05:13.047
"Of course!" the local painter exclaimed. "We'll take a look right now."

69
00:05:13.048 --> 00:05:15.241
The curator peered at the painting.

70
00:05:15.242 --> 00:05:21.225
"Oh, I remember this one," she said. "It was one of my favorites."

71
00:05:21.226 --> 00:05:26.669
Henry stepped over to Daniella. "Thanks for helping my friend," he told her.

72
00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:29.978
"Even though you didn't want to be recognized."

73
00:05:29.979 --> 00:05:42.033
Daniella winked. "Anything for art, my boy."

74
00:05:42.034 --> 00:05:46.786
"Wow," Henry said later as the curator hung up Nathan's painting.

75
00:05:46.787 --> 00:05:48.887
"It looks great!"

76
00:05:48.888 --> 00:05:54.080
Nathan looked stunned. "I can't believe my painting is in the museum!"

77
00:05:54.081 --> 00:06:00.244
Nora stared up at the painting. "Hi, Patches," she said sadly.

78
00:06:00.245 --> 00:06:03.845
"Don't worry." Nathan put an arm around her.

79
00:06:03.846 --> 00:06:07.030
"The painting is yours, just like I promised.

80
00:06:07.031 --> 00:06:10.668
The museum is just borrowing it for a year, okay?"

81
00:06:10.669 --> 00:06:14.934
"Mine! Hooray!" Nora cheered.

82
00:06:14.935 --> 00:06:20.808
Nathan laughed. "And hooray for The Lemonade Detectives!" he added.

83
00:06:20.809 --> 00:06:31.199
"They always solve the case—eventually!"
